id: caltrops
name: Caltrops
kind: gear
craftDC: Qualified
# Scattering them costs 1 Action, by the table's ruling: the entry gives no Action Cost.
placeCost: 1
# "Any Character (except those in a High Environment) who moves through any Square in that
# AoE has their Life Points reduced by 1d4(bT)." Rolled with the base Tier of Power of whoever
# moves through - the one suffering it, as with burning ground or a collision - by the
# table's ruling.
hazardDice: 1d4
hazardScale: bT
hazardSparesAirborne: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Spikes scattered across the ground. Anyone moving through them loses 1d4(bT) Life Points.
text: >
  Caltrops: A handful of spikes you scatter across the ground to prevent pursuit.
  –Craft DC: Qualified
  –Effects: Select a Square within a Destructive Sphere AoE (centered on you). Create a
  Sphere AoE centered on that Square. Any Character (except those in a High Environment) who
  moves through any Square in that AoE has their Life Points reduced by 1d4(bT). This effect
  does not stack if they move through multiple Squares.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Scattering them puts a card in the chat. Anyone who moves through the spikes presses its
# button for their own character, and loses the Life Points: 1d4 per base Tier of Power of
# theirs, rolled, and taken off as a Life Point reduction - past Soak and Damage Reduction,
# since it is not Damage. In a High Environment the button says so and takes nothing.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where they are. There are no Squares here: which Square, and who the Sphere covers, are the
# table's, and so is who moved through it - which is why the button is pressed rather than
# anything firing by itself.
#
# "This effect does not stack if they move through multiple Squares." One press for one
# movement through the spikes, however many of their Squares it crossed. That is the
# player's to keep, the way the Squares are.
#
# How long they stay down, and whether they are used up, the entry does not say. The card
# stays in the chat and the Caltrops stay on the character, for the table to decide.
